333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Industrial output and transportation systems had to work together</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Factory output alone guaranteed victory</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Fuel and ports were unnecessary</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Codebreaking replaced supplies</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L05_Q16 A01 Multiple causes</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L05_Q16</p><div style="border:3px solid #7c3aed;background:#f5f3ff;padding:10px;text-align:center"><h3>Interacting causes—not inevitability</h3><p><span style="background:#fee2e2;padding:4px">Postwar settlement</span> + <span style="background:#fef3c7;padding:4px">economic crisis</span> + <span style="background:#dcfce7;padding:4px">authoritarian expansion</span> + <span style="background:#dbeafe;padding:4px">militarism</span></p><p>failure of collective security + appeasement + territorial ambition + political decisions</p><p style="font-size:20px">↓</p><p><b>Escalating aggression → invasion of Poland → wider war</b></p><p><small>Alternative choices remained possible; arrows show contribution, not automatic destiny.</small></p></div><p>Which explanation is strongest?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 5 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>War grew from interacting conditions and decisions, including expansion, failed deterrence, appeasement, and alliance choices</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Munich alone automatically caused every theater</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>One leader controlled every decision worldwide</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Economic crisis had one identical political result</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L05_Q17 A02 Chronology</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L05_Q17</p><table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><caption><strong>World War II chronology</strong></caption><tr style="background:#fde68a"><th>Year</th><th>Events</th></tr><tr><td>1938</td><td>Munich Agreement</td></tr><tr><td>1939</td><td>Germany invades Poland; wider European war begins</td></tr><tr><td>1940</td><td>Fall of France; Battle of Britain</td></tr><tr><td>1941</td><td>Operation Barbarossa; Pearl Harbor</td></tr><tr><td>1942–43</td><td>Midway; Stalingrad</td></tr><tr><td>1944</td><td>D-Day</td></tr><tr><td>1945</td><td>Germany and Japan surrender</td></tr></table><p>Why was 1941 a major expansion of the conflict?</p>]]></text><